/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFL003-M3 -- kOmegaSST, integrated to the wall (y+ ~ 1).

  THE MODEL IS PINNED A PRIORI TO kOmegaSST, AND THE REASON IS PURELY
  METHODOLOGICAL, never the arm ranking or proximity to the target.  kOmegaSST
  natively integrates through the viscous sublayer without the wall-damping
  functions the low-Re k-epsilon variants require, so a single, honest,
  well-posed wall-resolved model exists without introducing damping-function
  degrees of freedom.  This is standard OpenFOAM low-Re practice for a mesh
  with y+ ~ 1.  "kOmegaSST OR low-Re kEpsilon" is deliberately NOT left open:
  choosing among candidate models after seeing results is model-shopping, and
  M3 carries exactly one model, fixed before compute (PREREGISTRATION.md
  section 2).

  CONTAMINATION NOTE.  VMFL003-M2 ARM D also ran kOmegaSST, but with the log-law
  wall FUNCTION (nutkWallFunction), and its finest-level Delta p is on the
  permanent record.  M3 is a DIFFERENT configuration -- kOmegaSST integrated to
  the wall (nutLowReWallFunction, k LowRe, y+ ~ 1 mesh) -- whose answer has
  never been computed or seen.  The M3 model choice is therefore NOT inherited
  from arm D's ranking; arm D's value is cited in the pre-registration only as
  the state-(b) prior-art diagnosis that motivates trying wall resolution.

  COEFFICIENTS.  kOmegaSST's default constant set (Menter 2003) is used as
  shipped in OpenFOAM v2606
  (src/TurbulenceModels/turbulenceModels/RAS/kOmegaSST); the model has a large
  blended coefficient set and is left at its documented library defaults, with
  printCoeffs on so the run log records the set actually used.  This is the
  honest reading of "the standard SST model".
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      turbulenceProperties;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

simulationType  RAS;

RAS
{
    RASModel        kOmegaSST;
    turbulence      on;
    printCoeffs     on;
}

// ************************************************************************* //
